  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_006: scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) achieves 0.653 acc. The largest single gain came from multiprofile + scvi_n200 (0.520→0.653), and aggregation choice (avgpool vs transformer) showed negligible difference (0.650 vs 0.653). However, the scgpt RNA encoder has never been tested, leaving a major uncertainty about whether an alternative learned RNA representation could surpass scvi_n200. Question: config_009 (scgpt, multiprofile, transformer) isolates the encoder effect by changing only the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding profile (multiprofile) and aggregation (transformer) constant, enabling a direct head-to-head comparison with config_006. Why this is the best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving whether scgpt is competitive with or superior to scvi_n200 is the highest-value uncertainty. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new branch of multimodal experiments; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and can redirect budget toward multimodal fusion or image-encoder upgrades with confidence in the RNA side."
}

